{
  "$comment": "Canonicalizer selftest (design D6/PR-4) — the cross-language contract artifact. Both canonicalizer implementations (Python conformance/runner/canonical.py; TS conformance-runner/src/canonical.ts) must pass every case: conformance/tests/test_canonical_selftest.py iterates this file on the Python side, a vitest suite on the TS side (D12/TS-3). Case kinds: 'value' — parse input_json, canonicalize, compare to 'canonical' by string equality; 'error' — same via the rule-6 error canonicalization (message/suggestion/fix stripped at known levels only); 'interactions' — same via the rule-9 unordered-group sort; 'headers' — headers_contain vs actual_headers subset/pattern match must equal 'matches'; 'reject' — canonicalization of the input (input_json, or a non-finite double named by 'special') must raise/throw. input_json is a raw JSON text string so number tokens survive the container file's own parsing: the harness MUST parse it with a loader that preserves the int-vs-float token distinction (Python json.loads; TS lossless number capture per D6 rule 3 — plain JSON.parse would collapse 18.0 to 18 and fail the float-token cases by design).",
